{{!--
  about.hbs — cargo-about Handlebars template for THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
  ===========================================================================
  Rendered by `cargo about generate --all-features about.hbs` (config:
  about.toml). Produces the RUST-CRATE slice of the repo-root
  THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md — one entry per license in the LOCKED dependency graph
  (Cargo.lock), listing the crates under it, with the verbatim license text.

  IMPORTANT — this template owns ONLY the Rust-crate section. The full file is
  ASSEMBLED by scripts/desktop/gen-third-party-notices.sh, which sandwiches this
  rendered output between a static header and the static
  "UI / npm dependencies" + "Bundled binaries" (Chromium/Node/patchright)
  sections (those are BINARIES / npm packages, invisible to cargo-about). Do NOT
  add the surrounding document chrome here — the assembler owns it so the two
  halves cannot drift.

  DATA MODEL (cargo-about 0.6.x, the `handlebars` Rust crate):
    {{overview}}  — array of { name, id, count } per license (summary counts).
    {{licenses}}  — array of { name, id, text, used_by: [ { crate: {name,
                    version, repository, ... } } ] }.
  NOTE: this handlebars engine does NOT expose `.length` on arrays as a path
  (it errors hard: "Cannot access array/vector with string index"), so we never
  index array lengths — we only iterate with {{#each}} and print scalar fields.
  The `gt`/`or` helpers cargo-about registers ARE available and used on the
  scalar `count` in the overview.
--}}
{{!--
  Verbatim fields (license name/text) use TRIPLE mustache {{{ }}} to DISABLE
  handlebars' default HTML-entity escaping — legally the license text must be
  reproduced verbatim, and {{text}} would turn `"`→`&quot;`, `<`→`&lt;`, `=`→
  `&#x3D;`, corrupting it. `id` and `crate.*` are simple ASCII SPDX/name/version
  strings, so double-mustache is fine for them.
--}}
{{#each overview}}
- **{{{name}}}** (`{{id}}`) — {{count}} crate{{#if (gt count 1)}}s{{/if}}
{{/each}}

{{#each licenses}}
### {{{name}}} (`{{id}}`)

Used by:

{{#each used_by}}
- `{{crate.name}}` {{crate.version}}{{#if crate.repository}} — {{crate.repository}}{{/if}}
{{/each}}

<details><summary>License text — {{{name}}}</summary>

```
{{{text}}}
```

</details>

{{/each}}
